e/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/claude-rc1-09.verdict.txt:36:Minimal fix: have the Bash guard treat a reference to _night_mode_parts in a -c/-e body the same way it treats a reference to the toggle script. Or declare this residual next to NF-08b.\n.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/payload-rc1-29.redacted.txt:72:[Omitted long matching line]\n.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/claude-rc1-10.verdict.txt:1:PAYLOAD 10/32: v1.4.3-rc.1..0e687e3c5285. Files: _night_mode_parts/toggles.py, _pair_rail_parts/{__init__,_shared,part_01..04}.py, _policy_parts/{__init__,decisions,loading,predicates,yaml_blocks,yaml_flows,yaml_scalars}.py, _precompact_parts/{__init__,ledger_index}.py. All files are new; each is code moved out of a facade.\n.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/claude-rc1-10.verdict.txt:16:- Condition 5: _KERNEL_PATHS has 123 string rows. _policy_parts/**/* and _pair_rail_parts/**/* are among them, with the five flat modules and adapters/live. The precompact and night-mode facades were never kernel, so their parts packages correctly stay outside the list. Conditions 7, 9 and 10 hold against this code: the kit's check_instrument refuses a triple absent from the manifest and a malformed sha.\n.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/claude-rc1-10.verdict.txt:23:P1 — .claude/hooks/_lib/_pair_rail_parts/part_01.py:477-486, with CHANGELOG.md:191.\n.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/claude-rc1-10.verdict.txt:42:4. _policy_parts/__init__.py:15 and _precompact_parts/__init__.py:16 exec the part sources, so each part's module docstring is stored into the facade's __doc__. At runtime _lib.policy.__doc__ and check_precompact_continuity.__doc__ become one-line part docstrings, which hides the contract text from help()/introspection. The parts are also recompiled from source in every process, with no .pyc. Neither has a functional effect. Fix: restore __doc__ after install, or drop the part docstrings.\n.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/diff-rc1-20.patch:2683:+   `_lib/_policy_parts/`, ...), each